go 1.27.1

// Every module in the repository, listed explicitly.
//
// Do NOT run `go work use -r .` here. The tree contains two devenv
// environments under internal/services/*/.devenv, whose state/go/pkg/mod is a
// Go module cache. A recursive walk treats every one of those cached modules as
// a workspace module and the build fails with "module X appears multiple times
// in workspace". Listing the six modules by hand is what keeps the workspace
// equal to the repository.
//
// The platform services are listed because they are part of this workspace, not
// because they should build against it. `make services-vet` and
// `make services-test` set GOWORK=off so each service is built and tested on its
// own go.mod, the same way it is deployed. The build graph being shared and the
// dependency graph being independent are both deliberate: a service that could
// only build inside this workspace could not be released on its own.
use (
	.
	./contracts
	./internal/services/aggregator-service
	./internal/services/product-listing-service
	./internal/services/product-search-service
	./internal/services/product-service
)
